rows.en:
You know how it goes on a test of courage: one person gets scared and starts running, and then everybody gets scared and starts running too, right?
And whoever ends up last gets hit by this feeling that something's closing in behind them.
So everyone runs like mad, fighting to get ahead so they won't be the one stuck at the back... It was like that.{p}

When we got outside, it hit me all over again how good fresh air could taste.
Once we were out in the schoolyard, we took the deepest breaths we could.
Like we were trying to breathe out every last bit of that stinking air we'd sucked in.{p}

When I came to, I was lying in my own futon.
...I'd been dreaming.
That's right... Iwayama still hadn't come back to school since that night...{p}

When I looked closer, Hino's skin was crawling with faces, packed tight. The faces of the people he'd absorbed, most likely.
His Adam's apple, his cheeks and neck, his forehead... At this rate, his whole body {f:had to be|must be} the same.
Each of the faces {f:seemed|seemed} to be babbling some garbled thing at {f:me|me}.{p}

Then, all of a sudden, my whole body felt light.
The merging {f:seemed|seemed} to be over.
{f:I|I} slowly opened my eyes.{p}

With that, Mr. Shirai left.
...Is it really the way he said{f:|}?
Just then, a voice echoed in {f:my|my} head.{p}

It's embarrassing to admit, but my life matters more to me than a newspaper article.
Well, it's not like I came away with nothing.
If I'd wanted to, I could've written an article about that jelly thing.{p}

{f:I|I} turned off the light like he told me.
Evening was already over, and the air had the feel of night.
With the light off, it was pitch dark{f:|}.{p}

The first to speak was Fukuzawa{f:|}.
"H-hey.
Is it okay to turn the light on now...?"{p}

{f:I|I} answered.
"Yeah{f:|}, let's turn it on."
{f:I|I} stood up and took a step to go turn on the light.{p}

The light came on.
Fukuzawa had turned it on for us{f:|}.
Everyone was deathly pale.{p}
